  "strategy": "Optimization Strategy with Fourier Transform and Geometric Phasing for Step-Function Coefficient Search\n\nApproach and rationale:\nI'll implement a unique dual-phase optimization approach that combines:\n1. A structured geometric initialization with spectral optimization\n2. Hierarchical refinement using curvature-driven descent methods\n3. Anisotropic exploration of the frequency-space parameterization\n\nThe key innovations are:\n- Treating the step-function as a frequency-response surface\n- Using both linear and geometric programming for different scales\n- Implementing multilevel optimization with efficient FFT-based convolution\n- Maintaining explicit bounds between different execution stages\n\nMathematical Specification:\nFor a normalized sequence a of length n, we define the evaluation metric as:\nJ(a) = 2n\u00b7max(convolve_full(a,a)) / norm(a)^2\nwhere convolve_full is the linear convolution (full mode) producing 2n-1 coefficients.\n\nThe optimization will proceed by parameterizing the sequence as a truncated Fourier series:\na_k = sum_{m=1}^{M} A_\u00b7mean_M \uc54a\uc558\uc5b4\uc694",
